<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 3 July, from 987 to 1988.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">987 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,039 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hugh Capet is crowned King of the Franks</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hugh Capet was crowned, replacing the Carolingian line with his own family. The Capetians and their cadet branches would rule France almost without a break until 1848.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-de-champlain" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/samuel-de-champlain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1608 CE <span class="tih-ago">418 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Samuel de Champlain founds Quebec</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Samuel de Champlain established a fortified trading post at Quebec on the St Lawrence. It became the capital of New France and the heart of French-speaking North America, a culture that endures in Canada today.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/french-empire">French Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-de-champlain">Samuel de Champlain</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-france">New France</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1754 CE <span class="tih-ago">272 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Washington surrenders Fort Necessity to the French</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Outnumbered and rain-soaked, the 22-year-old Washington surrendered Fort Necessity in western Pennsylvania. It was the only surrender of his military career and an opening clash of the French and Indian War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1863 CE <span class="tih-ago">163 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pickett's Charge fails on the final day of Gettysburg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 12,500 Confederates advanced across open fields against the Union centre on Cemetery Ridge and were cut down. The repulse ended Lee's invasion of the North and is often called the high-water mark of the Confederacy.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1886 CE <span class="tih-ago">140 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Karl Benz drives his Motorwagen in public in Mannheim</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Karl Benz made the first public drive of his three-wheeled Patent-Motorwagen on the Ringstrasse in Mannheim. Patented that January, it is widely regarded as the first practical petrol-powered motor car.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ringstrasse">Ringstrasse</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1988 CE <span class="tih-ago">38 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">USS Vincennes shoots down Iran Air Flight 655</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The US cruiser Vincennes, mistaking the Airbus for an attacking fighter, shot down Iran Air Flight 655 over the Persian Gulf, killing all 290 on board. The tragedy deepened hostility between Washington and Tehran.</p></div></li></ol>
